{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_266u4mapsolibcavfcn4tvuvxwjbzj7tmgcwbldkogyamnkd5hea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte.** No divergences found; no fixes to `translation/src/lib.rs` were needed.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ `driver`, `print_foo` both exported; `ldd -r` clean |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes (randomized) | ✅ 20/20 rows, 0 unchecked |\n| Binary stdout comparison | ✅ N/A — no `[[bin]]` / `add_executable`; asserted by `cfg20_no_binary_target_exists` |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | ✅ 16/16 rows, 0 unchecked |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ 4 configs (default + `--no-default-features`) × (debug + release cdylib) |\n\n## The library\n\n`c_src/src/driver.c` — 43 lines, one bit-field struct, two exported functions, zero branches and zero error returns. `print_foo` has external linkage but isn't in the header, so it's part of the ABI and is tested as the low-level entry point.\n\n## What was actually verified\n\n- **Bit-field packing/extraction** — `x:2`, `y:3`, `b:1` share byte 0 (bits 0-1, 2-4, 5). Confirmed the Rust layout against the gcc disassembly of `driver`, including that gcc emits `movzbl; and $0x1` for the `_Bool` field, so a non-canonical `_Bool` byte keeps only bit 0. All 256 possible bytes in that parameter slot tested exhaustively (the `enum`-equivalent out-of-range FFI input).\n- **Silent truncation** — `x≥4` and `y≥8` are truncated, not rejected; tested to `UINT_MAX`, plus one-past-boundary (`x=4`, `y=8`).\n- **`print_foo` driven with raw 8-byte images** — all 256 storage bytes and randomized garbage in the padding bits 6-7 and padding bytes 1-3, asserting padding never leaks into output. `driver` leaves those bits uninitialized, so they're only reachable through the low-level entry point.\n- **Composed pipeline** (row 18) — asserts `driver(x,y,b,z)` ≡ `print_foo(pack(x,y,b,z))` in *both* implementations, not just C≡Rust per function.\n- **Null/wild pointer UB** (rows 13-14) — the C code has no null check; both `.so`s are run in forked children and asserted to die with the *same* signal (SIGSEGV), with a sanity test proving a valid pointer exits 0.\n\n## Two harness issues worth knowing about\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not build the `cdylib`.** The tests were silently falling back to a stale `target/release/libdriver.so`. `run_verification.sh` now builds the cdylib explicitly per profile and pins it via `RUST_DRIVER_SO`.\n2. **libtest's own progress output collided with the fd-1 capture.** Comparing `printf` output requires redirecting the process-global fd 1, so a parallel test thread's `ok` got spliced into captured bytes and produced a bogus \"divergence\". Fixed via `RUST_TEST_THREADS = \"1\"` in `.cargo/config.toml` (needed by anyone running these tests) plus flushing Rust's `stdout` before each capture.\n\nI also confirmed the suite has teeth: injecting a wrong mask (`y & 0xF` instead of `0x7`) made 4 tests fail with precise diagnostics; the mutation was reverted and the full sweep re-run green. `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the `build/` directory.\n\nNote the registry was unreachable, so `libloading`/`libc` resolve from the local cargo cache; `.cargo/config.toml` sets `net.offline = true` accordingly — drop that line if you have network access."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":72332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1744,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1419a3b-9b9b-4f7d-8e2a-1d8bc959f7a0","uuid":"ac1c7066-9be2-4c71-8921-cde1ea09b497","timestamp":"2026-09-05T05:11:51.961Z"}
